title: message panel
tags: Panel [[Panel types]]
kind: reference
aliases: message messages
summary: The workspace's message log, newest first: every status message, every command run, the output of shell lines and scripts, the daemon's reports.

Open it with `panel:set type message` (<<key "panel:set type message" "t g">>). It
shows what the workspace's message log holds, each line with its time, the newest at
the ''top'':

* every message shown in the status bar, which it keeps after the next one replaced it ([[Status bar and task bar]]);
* every command run in the workspace, as `> name arguments`, written before it runs ([[Commands]]);
* a shell line as `$ command`, its output line by line, and `[exit N]` when it failed ([[Bash mode]]);
* the summary of a reconcile, of a duplicate scan, of an orphan detection;
* what a script posts with `mf gui message`, and the output of a script started with `script:run`;
* the daemon's warnings about the workspace's repository ([[Connection to the daemon]]).

A new line is added at the top. The view stays there as long as you are reading the
top; once you have scrolled down into older lines, it does not move.

`message:clear`, or the panel's ''Clear'' button, empties the log. Each workspace has
its own, and none outlives the session.
